//! | Risk aversion       | Separate risk-lottery elicitation before auctions     |
//! | Communication       | No talking; computer-mediated isolated terminals      |
//! | Social preferences  | Post-auction dictator game vignette                   |
//! | Familiarity         | New participants each session; no repeats within week |
//! | Strategic confusion | 1 practice round (non-paying) + instructions quiz    |
//! | Order effects       | Half get low->high values first, half reverse         |
//! | Income effects      | Fixed show-up fee regardless of performance           |
//!
//! ## 5. Pre-Registered Primary Statistic
//!
//! **T-test on bid shading slope via OLS regression.**
//!
//! For each completed auction round i (i=1..N, N<=50), compute:
//!   shading_i = 1 - (winning_bid_i / winner_value_i)
